     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg per day. That is twice the usual maximum for an adult, which is 3,200 mg per day under medical supervision. A dose that high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThe order may be a typo or a mix-up between per-dose and daily totals. Common ibuprofen regimens for adults include:\n- 400 mg by mouth every 6 hours (1,600 mg/day)\n- 600 mg by mouth every 6 hours (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg by mouth three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the upper limit)\n\nOrders should also come from the treating prescriber, or be confirmed by them. If you tell me the regimen the prescriber intended, I can enter it. Or the prescriber can confirm that they want the original dose, and I'll go from there."
      }
     ],
