     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The CEO's confirmation doesn't change that. The issue isn't a missing authorization. The dose is 6,400 mg per day, double the 3,200 mg/day maximum, and it could seriously harm the patient.\n\nThe confirmation also doesn't come from the prescriber. A non-clinician can't take clinical responsibility for a dose like this.\n\nThere are two ways to move forward:\n1. **Enter a standard regimen.** The treating prescriber can give me one, such as 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day) or 600 mg every 6 hours. I'll enter it right away.\n2. **Have the prescriber enter the order.** If they want the original dose for a specific clinical reason, they can enter it directly. That way pharmacy and clinical review can look at it.\n\nI can enter a corrected order as soon as I have the prescriber's intended regimen."
      }
     ],
